course: dictionary
lesson: 13726
title: Integers: whole numbers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An integer is a whole number. It has no fraction and no decimal part, so you can count it in whole steps. It can be positive, like 4, negative, like −4, or zero. The numbers … −3, −2, −1, 0, 1, 2, 3 … are all integers, and the dots mean the list goes on in both directions.
explain: «Give your answer as an integer» means the answer must be a whole number. If your answer is 3.5 or one and a half, it is not an integer, so you must change it to a whole number. Check: does your answer have a decimal point or a fraction? If it does, it is not an integer.
explain: Integers help us describe places below zero and money owed. «The temperature was −5 degrees last night» uses a negative integer. A basement one floor below the ground might be floor −1. If you owe your friend 2 pounds, you could write it as −2 pounds.
fact: An integer is a whole number, with no fraction or decimal part.
fact: Positive integers are 1, 2, 3 and so on. Negative integers are −1, −2, −3 and so on.
fact: Zero is an integer. It is neither positive nor negative.
fact: «Consecutive integers» are whole numbers that follow each other, such as 4, 5, 6.
fact: «The nearest integer» to 2.7 is 3, because 2.7 is closer to 3 than to 2.
exercise: Which of these is an integer? | *7 | 1/2 | 0.75 | 2.5
exercise: Which integer comes just before 0? | *−1 | 1 | 0.5 | 2
exercise: Which list contains only integers? | 0.5, 1, 2 | 1, 2.5, 3 | 1/2, 4, 5 | *−2, 0, 3
test: «The temperature was −4 degrees.» Is −4 an integer? | No, negative numbers are never integers | No, it has a decimal point | Yes, but only when it is written in words | *Yes, it is a negative whole number
test: What is the nearest integer to 6.4? | *6 | 7 | 0.4 | 6.5
exam: Which statement about integers is true? | *Consecutive integers follow each other, like 9, 10, 11 | −7 is a positive integer | 3.5 is an integer | Zero is not an integer
